The bug is, whenever the player is hit by a touching attack, they are
immediately sent to the oracle level, regardless of what the monster
was -- even if they have the Amulet of Yendor, or even if they're on
the Astral Plane and get hit by a Rider (in which case the game has
some trouble since it has already deleted the oracle level data.)

Here's the offending code from the diff file:

                     case AT_TUCH:
      ! //BEGIN PACMAN CHALLENGE CODE
      !                       if(strcmp("Blinky", Monnam(mtmp))
      !                               || strcmp("Pinky", Monnam(mtmp))
      !                               || strcmp("Inky", Monnam(mtmp))
      !                               || strcmp("Clyde",
Monnam(mtmp)))
      !                       {
    //Do stuff, such as send the player to the Oracle

The problem is that when two strings are equal, strcmp returns 0; when
they are non-equal, it returns non-zero.  Each of those strcmps needs
to be a !strcmp.

Hopefully this will be fixed soon, and we can begin playing normally.



